  "title": "Gameplay Atlas: Care & Sustain",
  "date": "2026-11-18T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Gameplay Atlas: Care & Sustain\n\nRecently, I found this website made by @onefifthblue.\nIt disassembles small mechanics from games across different genres.\nSometimes when I decide to make a game,\nmaking one mechanic is not hard.\nBut one mechanic cannot fit the scale of a modern game.\nThinking through multiple mechanics takes time and energy.\nThat is where this website comes in.\nIt is like a dictionary,\nso this series will start reading and collecting these core mechanics.\n\nLet's start with \"Care and Sustain\":\n\nTopics\n\nUnder the theme of \"Care and Sustain\" are farming, fishing, cooking, mining, survival, and breeding.\n\nThey are like resource management: keeping plants and land healthy, kitchen preparation, and maintaining mental health...\n\nFarming\n\nCore loops:\n\nGround and planting\n\nAdd seasons (timeline)\n\nIrrigation coverage (toolkit upgrade)\n\nFertilizer investment (toolkit upgrade)\n\nSeed reinvestment\n\nCrop–substrate matching (match the soil with the plant)\n\nCrop protection\n\nLivestock care\n\nThe site introduced several games as examples:\n\nStardew Valley\nStardew Valley\n\nCore Keeper\nCore Keeper\n\nDinkum\nDinkum\n\nTerraria\nTerraria\n\nFishing\n\nBite timing\n\nLine tension control\n\nTracking a moving fish (following the fish's movement so it doesn't drop the hook)\n\nFinding fish habitats\n\nBait loadouts (preparation, managing bait)\n\nChoosing a cast location\n\nPassive fishing traps\n\nFish-pond production\n\nTimed fishing contests\n\nThe examples are:\n\nGraveyard Keeper\nGraveyard Keeper\n\nDREDGE\nDREDGE\n\nCooking\n\nRecipe knowledge unlocks\n\nIngredient substitution (replace an expensive ingredient and still get the same food)\n\nCooking completion windows\n\nStaged preparation and assembly\n\nTimed order triage\n\nKitchen station handoffs\n\nMeal buff loadouts (preparation)\n\nPreservation through processing\n\nMeasured ingredient dosing\n\nTargeted flavor scoring\n\nThe examples are:\n\nBattle Chef Brigade Deluxe\nBattle Chef Brigade Deluxe\n\nCooking Simulator\nCooking Simulator\n\nBrewmaster: Beer Brewing Simulator\nBrewmaster: Beer Brewing Simulator\n\nDon't Starve Together\nDon't Starve Together\n\nThe Long Dark\nThe Long Dark\n\nPlateUp!\nPlateUp!\n\nOvercooked! 2\nOvercooked! 2\n\nValheim\nValheim\n\nMining\n\nMining is quite like survival; the two themes share some mechanics.\n\nHarvesting tool gates (you need the right tool to start)\n\nResource detection overlays\n\nVolumetric excavation\n\nOxygen-budgeted gathering\n\nGathering quotas and stopping decisions\n\nGathering to sustain gathering\n\nClues to buried deposits\n\nDismantling for salvage (reusing tools as resources)\n\nRevisiting renewable forage\n\nDepth-targeted mining (different depths yield different resources)\n\nThe examples are:\n\nTerraria\nTerraria\n\nASTRONEER\nASTRONEER\n\nNo Man's Sky\nNo Man's Sky\n\nSubnautica\nSubnautica\n\nDAVE THE DIVER\nDAVE THE DIVER\n\nDeep Rock Galactic\nDeep Rock Galactic\n\nSurvival & needs\n\nCompeting survival needs\n\nCollecting and purifying water\n\nFatigue and sleep planning\n\nBleeding and urgent bandaging\n\nWound hygiene and infection prevention\n\nInspecting the body to find problems (watch out for insects or viruses)\n\nFood balance and nutrition\n\nStress buildup and crisis\n\nWetness, cold, and warming up\n\nInjured limbs change capabilities\n\nTemporary symptom relief\n\nInterrupting disease transmission\n\nThe examples are:\n\nGreen Hell\nGreen Hell\n\nProject Zomboid\nProject Zomboid\n\nRimWorld\nRimWorld\n\nDarkest Dungeon\nDarkest Dungeon\n\nKenshi\nKenshi\n\nOxygen Not Included\nOxygen Not Included\n\nBreeding & ecology\n\nThis is like farming, but with hybridization.\n\nArranging neighbors to breed plants\n\nSelecting parents for offspring traits\n\nPreserving genetic diversity\n\nGradually taming wild animals\n\nControlling breeding and population size\n\nChecking habitat capacity before adding animals\n\nPlanning which species can share a home\n\nPreparing conditions that enable breeding\n\nThe examples are:\n\nNiche - a genetics survival game\nNiche - a genetics survival game\n\nRust\nRust\n\nPlanet Zoo\nPlanet Zoo\n\nMegaquarium\nMegaquarium",
